From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Ericson <John.Ericson@Obsidian.Systems>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 01:48:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ipadm: give the ofmt callback the signature its own typedef
 declares

`print_prop_cb` is declared through `ofmt_cb_t`:

    static ofmt_cb_t print_prop_cb;                       /* ipadm.c:219 */
    typedef boolean_t ofmt_cb_t(ofmt_arg_t *, char *, uint_t);
                                            /* libofmt/common/ofmt.h:171 */

but defined taking a `size_t`:

    static boolean_t
    print_prop_cb(ofmt_arg_t *ofarg, char *buf, size_t bufsize)

On LP64 those are different types -- eight bytes against four -- so this is a
real conflict, not a spelling difference. It has been benign in practice
because the value is a small buffer size and the ABI passes both in the same
register, but the declaration and the definition disagree, and a compiler is
entitled to say so. Ones that enforce it do:

    error: conflicting types for 'print_prop_cb'; have
        'boolean_t(ofmt_arg_t *, char *, size_t)'

`print_prop()`, which is only called from that callback and forwards the same
argument, changes with it -- along with the `propsize` it passes to
`ipadm_get_ifprop()`, `ipadm_get_prop()` and `ipadm_get_addrprop()`. All
three take `uint_t *`, so `&propsize` on a `size_t` handed them a pointer to
an eight-byte object they write four bytes of, leaving the upper half as
whatever the initialiser left behind.

No functional change: every value involved is bounded by MAXPROPVALLEN.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 usr/src/cmd/cmd-inet/usr.sbin/ipadm/ipadm.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/usr/src/cmd/cmd-inet/usr.sbin/ipadm/ipadm.c b/usr/src/cmd/cmd-inet/usr.sbin/ipadm/ipadm.c
index 17481bc4b7..022577c34f 100644
--- a/usr/src/cmd/cmd-inet/usr.sbin/ipadm/ipadm.c
+++ b/usr/src/cmd/cmd-inet/usr.sbin/ipadm/ipadm.c
@@ -733,13 +733,13 @@ do_disable_if(int argc, char *argv[], const char *use)
  * Print individual columns for the show-*prop subcommands.
  */
 static void
-print_prop(show_prop_state_t *statep, uint_t flags, char *buf, size_t bufsize)
+print_prop(show_prop_state_t *statep, uint_t flags, char *buf, uint_t bufsize)
 {
 	const char		*prop_name = statep->sps_pname;
 	char			*ifname = statep->sps_ifname;
 	char			*propval = statep->sps_propval;
 	uint_t			proto = statep->sps_proto;
-	size_t			propsize = MAXPROPVALLEN;
+	uint_t			propsize = MAXPROPVALLEN;
 	ipadm_status_t		status;
 
 	if (statep->sps_ifprop) {
@@ -772,7 +772,7 @@ cont:
  * Callback function for show-*prop subcommands.
  */
 static boolean_t
-print_prop_cb(ofmt_arg_t *ofarg, char *buf, size_t bufsize)
+print_prop_cb(ofmt_arg_t *ofarg, char *buf, uint_t bufsize)
 {
 	show_prop_state_t	*statep = ofarg->ofmt_cbarg;
 	const char		*propname = statep->sps_pname;
